== Music ==
* The stage's [[music]] is called ''Mater Prope'' or ''Nativitate''.<ref>[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/album/the-binding-of-isaac-afterbirth-ost Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth OST]</ref>
** These names are in Latin and could be translated to "Almost Mother" and "With Birth" / "Due to Birth" / "At the Time of Birth" respectively.
** ''Nativitate'' has a combat layer which can only be heard in rooms with enemies. Since enemies do not spawn on ??? normally, the only way to hear the combat layer is to encounter enemies in {{r|I AM ERROR}} rooms, {{r|Crawl Space}}s, rooms created by {{t|Blue Key}}, or {{r|Red Room}}s. Spawning enemies via [[Reward Plate]]s, however, will not change the music to the combat layer.
*** The layer can also be heard while playing [[DELETE THIS]] if the music is replaced with this floor's music track.
* The tracks that play during the battle against Hush are called ''Ascension'' (the {{e|???}} boss fight music; played during Hush's first phase, which is similar to the ??? boss) and ''Morituros'' (during the second phase).

== Trivia ==
* The displayed name of the chapter is ???, but the chapter is referred to as Blue Womb by the achievement, using the same logic as the character {{c|???}}.
* The character ??? and the chapter ??? have the same unlock requirements.
* ??? is unique as the only chapter that can be optionally done between mandatory chapters.
** {{dlc+|a+}} It is mandatory, however, to complete this chapter to unlock {{s|The Void}}.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} It is also mandatory to complete three times to unlock {{s|Downpour}}, as well as the rest of the alternative chapters.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|nr}} ??? is the smallest chapter, only containing 6 normally accessible rooms.
** {{s|Home}} ties with ??? in terms of having 6 normally accessible rooms.
* In [[Isaac's last will]], ??? is referred to as "some barren place".
** This may be a reference to the fact that infertile women were historically referred to as "barren".
* ???'s icon on the progress bar is actually a recolor of the {{s|Womb}}'s.
** Similarly, the trapdoor leading to ??? is a recolor of the trapdoor leading to the first and second floor of [[Chapter 4]].
* {{dlc+|r}} There is an unused version of ???, which uses the textures for the [[Basement]] and has the filter seen in [[Ascent|The Ascent]], with the song for [[The Void]]. The sound played after defeating Hush normally is replaced by a sound that plays after defeating an alt-path boss. Entering the trapdoor to {{s|Sheol}} or the beam of light to {{s|Cathedral}} after defeating Hush will send Isaac to {{s|Home}}. It can be accessed by typing <code>stage 9c</code> in the [[Debug Console]]. The void portal in this version of ??? is replaced by a cobweb.{{dlc-}}
* The 30-minute limit of reaching Blue Womb could signify how long it took Isaac to suffocate, hence the floor's theming and {{E|Hush}}'s presence.
* The Hush boss door's texture is larger than is depicted ingame. When the door sprite sheet is opened in a photo editor, it is revealed to actually be a archlike gateway, rather than the "garage door" like door it is seen as ingame.

